    <summary>Draw on your screen while you share it in a call, with the mouse, a pen, or your iPhone/iPad as a remote.</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[Glasspen Meet lets you draw on your screen while you share it in Zoom, Google Meet, Teams or any other call. Everyone sees your pen strokes, arrows, shapes and text on top of what you're presenting.

## Features
- Pen, highlighter, line, arrow, rectangle, ellipse, phone and person figures, text and eraser
- Strokes can fade after 1, 3 or 5 seconds, or stay until cleared
- Whiteboard mode to draw over a blank background
- Use your iPhone or iPad as a remote with the free Glasspen Remote app: zoom into a spot, then draw
- Lives in the tray; a small toolbar you can place at the bottom or on either side

## Shortcuts
- **Alt + `** (the key left of 1): start or stop drawing, from any app
- **Alt+1 … 0**: pick a tool and start drawing
- **Alt+Delete**: clear all
- **Esc**: stop drawing

The drawing and clear-all shortcuts can be changed in Settings.

## Notes
- Needs Windows 10 1809 or later, 64-bit.
- The first time it runs, allow it on **Private networks** so your phone can connect.
- Free and open source (MIT).
]]></description>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/toncatalansuazo/glass-meet-pen/releases/tag/v1.0.0-windows</releaseNotes>
  </metadata>
  <files>
    <file src="tools\**" target="tools" />
  </files>
</package>
